Usage: agent-deck mcp <command> [options]

Manage MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers for sessions.

Commands:
  list                List all available MCPs from config.toml
  attached [id]       Show MCPs attached to a session
  attach <id> <mcp>   Attach an MCP to a session
  detach <id> <mcp>   Detach an MCP from a session
  server <cmd>        Manage HTTP MCP servers (start/stop/status)

Examples:
  agent-deck mcp list                        # List available MCPs
  agent-deck mcp attached                    # Show MCPs for current session
  agent-deck mcp attached my-project         # Show MCPs for specific session
  agent-deck mcp attach my-project exa       # Attach exa to my-project (Codex uses global)
  agent-deck mcp attach my-project exa --global     # Attach globally
  agent-deck mcp detach my-project exa       # Detach exa from my-project
  agent-deck mcp server status               # Show HTTP server status
  agent-deck mcp server start slack          # Start HTTP server for slack MCP
